"""INNER PAGE — Contact us (route 'contact'). The paper form: a lined writing pad on a desk. Labels, placeholders and the typed input are all drawn as ink on paper (normal fonts only:
Inter, each word set at a slight angle and each letter with its own ink weight and baseline, so it reads as pen on paper without a novelty font). On send the page shows an in-page thank-you;
the form never opens an email app and has no mailto path. The endpoint is EMPTY by design and marked in src/page_contact.js (FORM_ENDPOINT): set it at real launch."""
import html
import pagekit as K
e = html.escape
NAME = 'contact'
TITLE = 'Contact'
CSS = 'page_contact.css'
JS = 'page_contact.js'
GLOBAL = 'FPContact'
TRADES = ['Siding', 'Windows', 'Shingle roofing', 'Metal roofing', 'Gutters', 'Exterior painting', 'Exterior doors', 'Garage doors', 'Patio covers', 'Storm damage']
